{"unit":5,"items":54,"pass":38,"title":"Unit Test · Unit 5","tracks":{"a54":"Track_5.4.mp3"},"SEGS":{"nyc":["a54",3.82,77.34]},"html":"\n  <section class=\"stage on\" data-stage=\"Unit Test\">\n    <div class=\"stage-head\">\n      <div class=\"kicker\">Unit 5 &middot; Unit Test</div>\n      <h2>On screen</h2>\n      <p>Six parts, <b>54 questions</b>, covering everything in Unit 5, with four questions that come back from Units 1&ndash;4. Answer them all, then press Check. You need <b>38 out of 54</b> to pass. Parts 7 and 8 are your writing and speaking &mdash; they are not marked automatically, but do not skip them. You can take this test as many times as you like.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"task\" data-task data-tid=\"review-u5\">\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 1 · VOCABULARY ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\">Part 1 &middot; Vocabulary &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 1&ndash;12</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the word that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">1</span><span class=\"body\">I guessed the ending after twenty minutes. The whole thing was completely&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">stunning</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">moving</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">predictable</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">2</span><span class=\"body\">The music stays with you for days. The&hellip; is the best part of the film.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">plot</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">soundtrack</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">cast</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">3</span><span class=\"body\">It is not a true story, but the setting feels completely real &mdash; very&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">authentic</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">harmless</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">accessible</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">4</span><span class=\"body\">He plays the same role in every film. His&hellip; in this one is no different.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">genre</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">scene</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">performance</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Which adjective is stronger? Match each ordinary adjective to its extreme partner.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">5&ndash;9</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"pairbox\">\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"g1\">bad</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"g2\">frightening</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"g3\">surprising</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"g4\">funny</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"g5\">annoying</button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"g3\" data-short=\"astonishing\">astonishing</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"g5\" data-short=\"infuriating\">infuriating</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"g1\" data-short=\"dreadful\">dreadful</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"g4\" data-short=\"hilarious\">hilarious</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"g2\" data-short=\"terrifying\">terrifying</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the adverb that can go with the adjective.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">10</span><span class=\"body\">The last twenty minutes are <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"absolutely\" data-why=\"Extreme adjectives take <b>absolutely</b>, never <i>very</i>.\"> brilliant.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">11</span><span class=\"body\">The first half hour is <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"incredibly\" data-why=\"An ordinary adjective takes <b>incredibly</b> or <i>very</i>.\"> slow.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">12</span><span class=\"body\">The film is sad in places, but <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"essentially\" data-why=\"<b>Essentially</b> = when you look at the whole thing.\"> it is a positive story.</span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 2 · GRAMMAR ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 2 &middot; Grammar &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 13&ndash;26</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">13</span><span class=\"body\">I would recommend&hellip; it in the original language.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">to watch</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">watching</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">watch</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">14</span><span class=\"body\">She tends&hellip; the book before she sees the film.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">to read</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">reading</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">read</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">15</span><span class=\"body\">I&hellip; that film three times, and I still cry at the end.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">saw</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">am seeing</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">have seen</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">16</span><span class=\"body\">It&hellip; at the box office when it was originally released in 1994.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">failed</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">has failed</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">was failing</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the verb in brackets into the correct form: <i>-ing</i> or <i>to</i> + verb.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">17</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>watch</i>) I really enjoy <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"watching\" data-why=\"<b>Enjoy</b> + <i>-ing</i>.\"> old thrillers on a Sunday.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">18</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>find</i>) They hope <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"to find\" data-why=\"<b>Hope</b> + <i>to</i> + verb.\"> an audience outside their own country.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">19</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>imitate</i>) Producers have stopped <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"imitating\" data-why=\"<b>Stop</b> + <i>-ing</i> = give up doing it.\"> Hollywood.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">20</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>make</i>) It is not worth <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"making\" data-why=\"<b>Be worth</b> + <i>-ing</i>.\"> a comedy for an international audience.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the correct tense.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">21</span><span class=\"body\">The rent&hellip; three times since I moved in.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">went up</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">has gone up</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">is going up</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">22</span><span class=\"body\">I&hellip; to the theatre twice last month.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">have been</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">have gone</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">went</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">23</span><span class=\"body\">The film from Korea <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"won\" data-why=\"A finished time (<i>in 2019</i>) takes the past simple: <i>won</i>.\"> the prize in 2019.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">24</span><span class=\"body\">I’d <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"recommend seeing\" data-why=\"<b>Recommend</b> takes the <i>-ing</i> form: <i>recommend seeing</i>.\"> it at the cinema.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Write the second sentence so that it means the same as the first.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">25</span><span class=\"body\">I started watching it in 2018 and I still watch it every year.<br>I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"have watched it since 2018|have been watching it since 2018|'ve watched it since 2018\" data-why=\"A period running up to now &rarr; present perfect + <b>since</b>.\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">26</span><span class=\"body\">It is much less depressing than it sounds.<br>It is <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"nothing like as depressing as it sounds|not nearly as depressing as it sounds\" data-why=\"<b>Nothing like as &hellip; as</b> = far less.\"></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 3 · READING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 3 &middot; Reading &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 27&ndash;34</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the whole text once before you answer anything.</p>\n\n      <article class=\"reading\">\n        <h3>The film nobody went to see</h3>\n        <p class=\"stand\">Some films fail on the day they open and become classics twenty years later. There is a pattern to it, and it is not the one people assume.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">A</span>Every industry has stories about the thing that was ignored and then adored. In cinema the pattern is common enough that distributors have a word for it: a title with no opening weekend and a very long tail. What such films tend to share is not brilliance that audiences failed to notice. It is a mismatch between what the marketing promised and what the film actually is.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">B</span>Consider a prison drama released in the autumn of 1994. The poster showed two men and a wall; the title was difficult to say and impossible to remember. Audiences who wanted an escape story got a long, quiet film about friendship, and audiences who would have loved a long, quiet film about friendship never went, because nothing told them it existed. It made back barely half of what it cost.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">C</span>What rescued it was repetition. Television networks bought it cheaply, because nobody wanted it, and then showed it constantly. Viewers who would never have chosen it found themselves halfway through it on a wet Sunday. Within ten years it was appearing at the top of public lists of the greatest films ever made, and it has stayed there ever since.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">D</span>Distributors draw an uncomfortable lesson. A film that recovers this way almost always does so because somebody kept putting it in front of people who had not asked for it. Streaming, which lets you watch anything but shows you only what it predicts you will like, may be very bad at exactly that. Nobody has stumbled into a film on a streaming service in the way that a whole generation stumbled into this one.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">27</span><span class=\"body\">According to paragraph A, films that fail and then succeed usually failed because\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">they were badly made</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">they were sold as something they were not</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">they were too short</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">28</span><span class=\"body\">Why did television networks buy the 1994 film cheaply?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">it had won a major prize</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">the director offered them a deal</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">nobody else wanted it</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">True, False, or Not given? Choose for each sentence.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">29</span><span class=\"body\">The film made a profit when it was first released. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph B: it made back <b>barely half</b> of what it cost.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">30</span><span class=\"body\">The writer says the film is the greatest ever made. <select data-answer=\"N\" data-why=\"The text says it appears at the top of <i>public lists</i>; the writer never gives an opinion.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">31</span><span class=\"body\">The film was released in the autumn. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Paragraph B: <b>the autumn of 1994</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"F\">False</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">32</span><span class=\"body\">The writer thinks streaming services help this kind of film. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph D: streaming <b>may be very bad</b> at exactly that.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Answer the last two questions about the whole text.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">33</span><span class=\"body\">In paragraph A, <i>a very long tail</i> means the film\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">kept finding an audience for years afterwards</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">was longer than most films</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">had a sequel</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">34</span><span class=\"body\">The writer&rsquo;s worry about streaming is that it\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">charges too much for old films</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">never shows you anything you did not already want</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">removes films after ten years</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 4 · LISTENING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 4 &middot; Listening &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 35&ndash;40</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the questions first. Then play the recording twice.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"player\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('nyc',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Three years in New York\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"wave\"></div>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><b>Navigate B1+ &middot; Audio 5.4</b>Original coursebook recording</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the notes with one word or a number.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">35</span><span class=\"body\">She has lived in New York for about <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"3|three\" data-why=\"About <b>three</b> years.\"> years.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">36</span><span class=\"body\">The rent has gone up <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"3|three\" data-why=\"It has gone up <b>three</b> times since she moved in.\"> times since she moved in.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">37</span><span class=\"body\">The person who was mugged was her best <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"friend\" data-why=\"Her best <b>friend</b> was mugged, not the speaker.\"> .</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">38</span><span class=\"body\">When she says &ldquo;I haven&rsquo;t been mugged yet&rdquo;, the word <i>yet</i> suggests she\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">is sure it will never happen</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">has forgotten about it</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">thinks it could still happen</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">39</span><span class=\"body\">Her overall attitude to the city is\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">positive, in spite of the problems</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">completely negative</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">undecided</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">40</span><span class=\"body\">The purpose of the whole recording is to\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">complain about landlords</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">weigh the good and the bad of one city</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">recommend somewhere to stay</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 5 · FUNCTIONAL LANGUAGE ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 5 &middot; Functional language &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 41&ndash;48</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">What would you say? Choose the phrase that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">41</span><span class=\"body\">You want to admit a weakness before you give a positive verdict.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">On balance, I would highly recommend it.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">It is not perfect: the first half hour is very slow.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Based on a novel by Stephen King&hellip;</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">42</span><span class=\"body\">You want to place the film against others of the same kind.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">It was released in 1994.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">Honestly, just watch it.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Compared with most prison dramas, it is far less interested in escape.</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">43</span><span class=\"body\">You want to recommend it, but with one condition attached.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">I would highly recommend it &mdash; although not if you want something short.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">It is absolutely brilliant.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">The cast is excellent.</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Where does each line belong?</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">44&ndash;47</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"sortbox\">\n          <div class=\"sortpool\"><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Review\">Despite failing at the box office, it has become a modern classic.</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Chat\">Honestly, just watch it. Trust me.</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Review\">On balance, I would highly recommend it.</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Chat\">It was rubbish, don&rsquo;t bother.</button></div>\n          <div class=\"sortcols\"><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Review\"><h5>A written review</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Chat\"><h5>A conversation</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div></div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the four parts of the review in order.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">48</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"order\" data-order=\"r3,r1,r4,r2\">\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"r1\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">Based on a novel and released in 1994, it tells the story of a banker sent to prison.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"r2\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">On balance I would recommend it &mdash; although not if you are looking for something short.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"r3\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">Some films get better the second time you watch them. This is one of them.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"r4\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">The cast is excellent, but the first half hour is incredibly slow.</span></button>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 6 · PUTTING IT TOGETHER ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 6 &middot; Putting it together &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 49&ndash;54</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the conversation. Two of these gaps come back from earlier units. <span class=\"pill-rec\">recycled</span></p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"chat\">\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Zhanna</b>Have you seen the Korean one everybody is talking about?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>Twice. I <select data-answer=\"have never seen\" data-why=\"Experience up to now, no finished time &rarr; present perfect.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>never saw</option><option>have never seen</option><option>am never seeing</option></select> anything quite like it.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Zhanna</b>When did you watch it the first time?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>I <select data-answer=\"watched\" data-why=\"A finished time is understood &rarr; past simple.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>have watched</option><option>watched</option><option>was watching</option></select> it on the plane in March.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Zhanna</b>Worth going to the cinema for?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>I would recommend <select data-answer=\"seeing\" data-why=\"<b>Recommend</b> + <i>-ing</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>to see</option><option>see</option><option>seeing</option></select> it on a big screen. It is <select data-answer=\"nothing like as\" data-why=\"<b>Nothing like as &hellip; as</b> = far less.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>nothing like as</option><option>far as</option><option>not so much</option></select> violent as people say.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Zhanna</b>My brother said it was slow.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b><select data-answer=\"That&rsquo;s a fair point,\" data-why=\"Concedes before disagreeing. <b>Recycled from Unit 1.</b>\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>He&rsquo;s completely wrong,</option><option>That&rsquo;s a fair point,</option><option>I couldn&rsquo;t agree more,</option></select> but only the first half hour. <select data-answer=\"While I was watching\" data-why=\"A long background action &rarr; past continuous. <b>Recycled from Unit 2.</b>\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>While I watched</option><option>While I was watching</option><option>While I had watched</option></select> it, I forgot I was on a plane at all.</div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" onclick=\"checkReview(this)\" style=\"margin-top:24px\">Check my answers</button>\n      <div class=\"res\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"reviewResult\" class=\"review-result\"></div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 7 · WRITING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Part 7 &middot; Writing &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">Write 120&ndash;140 words. Give yourself twenty minutes.</p>\n    <div class=\"opentask\" data-open data-tid=\"test-write\">\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <p class=\"ohint\"><b>The task.</b> Write a review of a film, series or game you know well, for somebody deciding whether to spend two hours on it. Open with a line that makes a claim. Give the facts. Say what is good and what is not. Compare it with something of the same kind. Finish with a verdict that has one condition attached. Do not tell the ending.</p>\n        <textarea placeholder=\"Some films&hellip;   Based on&hellip; and released in&hellip;   The cast is&hellip;   It is not perfect:&hellip;   Compared with&hellip;   On balance, I would&hellip;\" data-track></textarea>\n      </span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bubble useful\">\n      <div class=\"blab\">Your review must contain</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>one <b>present perfect</b> and one <b>past simple</b>, each doing its own job</li>\n        <li>one <b>-ing</b> form and one <b>infinitive with to</b> after a verb that demands it</li>\n        <li>one extreme adjective with <b>absolutely</b>, and one ordinary one with <b>incredibly</b> or <b>very</b></li>\n        <li>one comparison: <b>compared with&hellip; / nothing like as&hellip; as&hellip;</b></li>\n        <li>a verdict with a condition, not just a star rating</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 8 · SPEAKING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 8 &middot; Speaking &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <div class=\"opentask speak\" data-open data-tid=\"test-speak\">\n      <div class=\"sp-head\"><span class=\"sp-ic\">&#127908;</span>\n        <div><b>Speaking &mdash; recommend it, then defend it</b><span>Extended turn</span></div></div>\n      <p class=\"sp-task\"><b>Part A.</b> Recommend the same film, series or game out loud in ninety seconds, without reading what you wrote. <b>Part B.</b> Then answer: <i>why do some stories travel across borders and others stop at the first subtitle?</i></p>\n      <ul class=\"sp-list\">\n        <li>say when you first saw it, and how many times you have seen it since</li>\n        <li>one thing you enjoy <b>watching</b>, and one thing you hope <b>to see</b> next</li>\n        <li>at least two comparisons with something the listener knows</li>\n        <li>one honest weakness, admitted before the verdict</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"sp-lang\"><b>Use this language</b>I&rsquo;ve seen it three times &middot; I first watched it in&hellip; &middot; It&rsquo;s worth watching because&hellip; &middot; Compared with&hellip; &middot; It&rsquo;s nothing like as&hellip; as&hellip; &middot; On balance&hellip;</div>\n      <div class=\"rec\">\n        <div class=\"rec-row\">\n          <button class=\"rec-btn\" type=\"button\" onclick=\"recToggle(this)\" aria-label=\"Record your answer\" title=\"Record\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M12 14a3 3 0 0 0 3-3V6a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v5a3 3 0 0 0 3 3zm5-3a5 5 0 0 1-10 0H5a7 7 0 0 0 6 6.9V21h2v-3.1A7 7 0 0 0 19 11z\"/></svg></button>\n          <div class=\"rec-label\"><b>Record your answer</b><span>Press the microphone and speak</span></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-wave\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-time\">0:00</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"rec-takes\"></div>\n        <div class=\"rec-note\">Record it, play it back, then submit it for assessment.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Parts 7 and 8 &middot; Assessment</div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">These two parts are not marked automatically and they are not marked by you. Submit your writing and record your speaking, then your teacher &mdash; or the AI tutor &mdash; scores each part against the criteria below and writes the feedback.</p>\n    <div class=\"rubric-slot\">\n      <ul class=\"reqlist\">\n        <li>my first line makes a claim instead of describing the plot</li>\n        <li>I gave the facts once and did not retell the whole story</li>\n        <li>I admitted at least one weakness</li>\n        <li>my verdict has a condition attached to it</li>\n        <li>I did not give away the ending</li>\n        <li>I used the present perfect for experience and the past simple for a finished time</li>\n        <li>every <i>-ing</i> and every <i>to</i> + verb followed the right verb</li>\n        <li>I spoke without reading, and made at least two comparisons</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n"}